<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">
<policyconfig>

  <!--
    The Linux half of "the app never binds; the service does".

    The helper at /usr/libexec/artmoon-input-service refuses to act without administrator
    rights, and on Linux the app has no way to hand it privilege except through pkexec. This
    action is what makes that pkexec call silent: `allow_active` grants it to the local active
    session with no authentication, so the one approval the user gives is the one that placed
    this file and the helper — not one per device toggle.

    Placing this file is what requires the password. That is the moment to be thinking about
    what it grants: the active session may run exactly one program as root, and pkexec binds
    this action to it by the exec.path annotation below, so it cannot be pointed anywhere else.

    Why this is safe to grant, given the program takes input from an unprivileged process:
      - It validates every busid as a strict shape AND checks the device exists on this
        machine via /sys, so it will only ever act on hardware that is physically present.
        It does not trust the list its caller sends.
      - It keeps no state. It reconciles against the kernel's own view and forgets.
      - It is statically linked, so there is no library for anything to inject into.
      - It sets its own PATH before running anything, so `usbip` and `modprobe` cannot be
        redirected by the environment of whatever started it.

    Deliberately NOT `allow_any` or `allow_inactive`: a remote session, or a session nobody
    is sitting at, cannot use this. That distinction is the reason this is done with polkit
    rather than by making the helper setuid — which is also ruled out because the helper
    resolves `usbip` through PATH, and a setuid binary doing that is a root hole by design.
  -->
  <action id="org.artmoon.input-service.reconcile">
    <description>Share USB devices over the network</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to share USB devices</message>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>yes</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/libexec/artmoon-input-service</annotate>
  </action>

</policyconfig>
